# Party banter at the Wizard of Wines. Each node opens with an `if` gate: the node is eligible only while its
# condition holds. Party members speak only through interjections; a line plays if a matching member is present.

~ banter_wine_country
if flag.davian_met and not flag.winery_reclaimed
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: A whole winery, and not one bottle left whole. The druids smashed the lot. I've never hated anyone on behalf of a bottle before.
interject name:ilse_varga: Siege logic. Burn the stores, starve the garrison. They know what they're doing.
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: That's worse. I wanted them to be stupid.
endif
-> END

~ banter_ravens
if flag.davian_met and not flag.keepers_allied
interject tag:bookish: Lycanthropy, but ravens. The literature is very thin. I'd like it noted that I am being extremely restrained about asking them questions.
interject tag:blunt: Noted. Keep being restrained.
endif
-> END

~ banter_father_and_son
if flag.elvir_story_heard and not flag.martikovs_reconciled
interject name:hedda_ironvow: The old man grieves like stone weathers. Slowly, from the outside in, and he calls it standing firm.
interject name:ilse_varga: He sent two soldiers out and one came back. Every officer I ever served under did the same sums. Most of them blamed the one who came back.
endif
-> END

~ banter_stones
if flag.winery_stone_hiding_told and not flag.winery_stone_recovered
interject class:wizard: Three stones that make vines grow where nothing should. Payment for one winter's lodging. That wizard either loved wine more than anyone ever has, or the stones were the cheapest thing in his pockets.
interject tag:curious: Or he's coming back for the casks.
endif
-> END

~ banter_reconciled
if flag.martikovs_reconciled
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: Did you see the old man's face? When he gave Adrian the press? I'm not crying. It's the vinegar.
interject name:hedda_ironvow: Mm. It's the vinegar. Stone remembers. So do fathers, eventually.
endif
-> END

~ banter_wine_flows
if flag.winery_wine_flows
interject tag:cheerful: First real wine in this whole valley, and we're the reason. I'm going to be insufferable about this.
interject tag:blunt: You were already insufferable.
interject tag:cheerful: Now I'll have a reason.
endif
-> END

~ banter_kept_the_fee
if flag.winery_strongbox_kept
interject class:cleric: We took the old man's strongbox in a war he was losing. I'd like that remembered when we're being proud of ourselves.
interject class:rogue: Remembered. It was a very good lock, though.
endif
-> END

~ banter_keepers
if flag.keepers_allied
interject tag:curious: There's a raven on that fence. And that one. And that one. They've been following us since the winery.
interject name:silvain_aster: We have, technically, been adopted by a secret society of shapechanging birds. I'm writing it down before anyone can talk me out of it.
endif
-> END
